Text Notes 25160 26060 0    79   ~ 16
ASIL-D SAFETY CONCEPT + DC-LINK DISCHARGE VERIFICATION
Text Notes 25160 26320 0    60   ~ 0
safe state = 3-phase-open (ASC above overspeed); discharge vs ECE R100 / ISO 6469
Text Notes 25150 26750 0    60   ~ 0
1 lockstep S32K396 (ASIL-D core) runs torque path
Text Notes 25150 27050 0    60   ~ 0
2 FS26 Q&A watchdog + monitors -> FS0B (no SW)
Text Notes 25150 27350 0    60   ~ 0
3 FS0B&MCU_EN&RDY&FLT-latch -> DRV_EN = 3-ph open
Text Notes 25150 27650 0    60   ~ 0
4 FS1B strap -> LS ASC latch (HS strapped OFF)
Text Notes 25150 27950 0    60   ~ 0
5 flyback EN = MCU OR FS26-GPIO1 (ASC gate power)
Text Notes 25150 28250 0    60   ~ 0
6 3x hall + sum(I)=0 plausibility (torque path)
Text Notes 25150 28550 0    60   ~ 0
7 2x iso VDC senses >5% = fault, VOFS monitored
Text Notes 25150 28850 0    60   ~ 0
8 DESAT per switch (SiC <=1.9 us detect), latching
Text Notes 29350 26750 0    60   ~ 0
9 HVIL open = VDDIO/2 signature -> torque off (FW)
Text Notes 29350 27050 0    60   ~ 0
--- DISCHARGE ---
Text Notes 29350 27350 0    60   ~ 0
PASSIVE 12x 22k 2512-2W (6s x 2p = 66k): 56 s to 60 V
Text Notes 29350 27650 0    60   ~ 0
ACTIVE QDIS + 4x 470R 10W = 1.88k: 1.6 s to 60 V
Text Notes 29350 27950 0    60   ~ 0
E = 116 J @850 V - 32 J/res worst; 4XX: 220R/15k
Text Notes 29350 28250 0    60   ~ 0
VERIFY: MCU fires QDIS, watches BOTH VDC channels
Text Notes 29350 28550 0    60   ~ 0
RULE: never energize w/o the DISCHARGE BOARD fitted
